The code statements that lead to the bug are:
memcpy(req->response, pkg->buffer, req->response_size);
Reason:
The memcpy copies req->response_size bytes from the packet buffer regardless of the actual frame size (pkg->frame.size). When a short response arrives (frame size smaller than the expected response size), this reads beyond the valid data in the DMA pool buffer, causing a buffer over-read.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
size_t len = min_t(size_t, pkg->frame.size, req->response_size);
memcpy(req->response, pkg->buffer, len);
Reason:
By computing the minimum of the actual frame size and the expected response size, the copy length is limited to the valid data present in the packet. This prevents reading past the frame boundary into stale buffer contents.

